Midas touch could NOT be turn-offable, or else it would be too powerful a
weapon.  Fitting in with the story, it should be:

	cursed:   50 turns.
	uncursed: 500 turns.
	blessed:  permanent (but don't generate these, just greedy players).

It adds something we don't currently have:  no longer should you blindly
bless unknown scrolls in the hope they are enlightenment/genocide/enchant/etc.

It is effectively a destroy weapon scroll (leave armour untouched).  Player
is thus susceptible to missile attacks, and cannot throw anything (except
money :]) back.  Of course, she has a great hand-to-hand weapon...

